# Every deadline in the main sources, judged: tools/check/deadline-sites.py says what a site is and what each verdict
# means. <path> | <function> | <form> | <count> | <verdict> | <reason>. The question for each: what happens when the
# deadline fires as the bounded work returns (the timeout lands on another thread after the block returned and before
# the timeout's scope completed)? A new site, or one more in a function, fails until it is judged here. drops-result
# marks the sites whose caller acts on a result the deadline can drop: known faults, each to be fixed with a race test.
kuicksilver-bench/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/bench/MemoryBench.kt | endpointIdle | withTimeout | 2 | side-effect-free | harness bound: the timeout fails the run or the iteration, nothing of the library depends on the result
kuicksilver-http2/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http2/runtime/H2Runtime.kt | awaitAnswer | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | joins the stream's answered Deferred; the caller goes on either way, the answer stays in the stream
kuicksilver-http2/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http2/runtime/H2Runtime.kt | closeWithinBound | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | both branches end alike: a transport whose close completed as the bound fires is closed hard, and closeTransportOnce does nothing to a closed one
kuicksilver-http2/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http2/runtime/H2Runtime.kt | runHealthCheck | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | made-flag | a PING acknowledgement read as the bound fires is taken from acked.isCompleted, not from the dropped result (CHANGELOG: "a health PING answered as its bound fires keeps the connection")
kuicksilver-http2/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http2/runtime/H2Runtime.kt | timerLoop | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | the kick only wakes the loop, which reads the core's timers again on every turn; a kick dropped at the deadline is not needed
kuicksilver-http2/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http2/runtime/H2Runtime.kt | waitWithin | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | made-flag | moved is set as the wait returns: a window or written frame taken as the send-stall bound fires is progress, not a stall
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/runtime/H3Session.control.kt | readUni | timer | 1 | made-flag | the timer reads header.settled, which the reader sets when the type arrived; a header read as the timer fires is kept
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/runtime/H3Session.critical.kt | attemptUntilTheLimitIsLow | timer | 1 | completedWithin | the attempt stores its result before it returns, and the guard's cancel gives the stored result (the same store-before-return)
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/runtime/H3Session.kt | withinWtDeadline | select-cancel | 1 | completedWithin | the timer branch joins the cancelled block and returns its result when it completed all the same (CHANGELOG: "the WebTransport deadline keeps a CONNECT that completed after it was chosen")
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/runtime/H3Session.shutdown.kt | goAwayConfined | timer | 1 | made-flag | rejects only the heads still pending with the same reader; a head read meanwhile left pendingHeaders and is the application's
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/runtime/RequestStream.kt | handOver | select-cancel | 1 | side-effect-free | a flush cancelled because the transport closed: nothing is taken from anyone, and a flush that completed first is left as it is
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/runtime/ServerRequestStream.kt | readRequestStream | timer | 1 | made-flag | the head timer acts only while head.settled is false; the reader settles the head as it arrives, so a head read in time is kept
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/webtransport/WtSessionImpl.kt | endConnect | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | joins the capsule reader for the peer's FIN; peerFinished is read after the wait, not the dropped result (the writes use completedWithin since class-sweep)
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/webtransport/WtSessionImpl.kt | ended | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | joins the capsule reader before terminate, which runs either way
kuicksilver-interop/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/interop/H3Interop.kt | download | withTimeout | 1 | side-effect-free | harness bound: the timeout fails the run or the iteration, nothing of the library depends on the result
kuicksilver-interop/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/interop/HqInteropClient.kt | download | withTimeout | 1 | side-effect-free | harness bound: the timeout fails the run or the iteration, nothing of the library depends on the result
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/Errors.kt | awaitContent | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | made-flag | arrived is set as the wait returns: data that arrived as the socket timeout fires is read, not a SocketTimeoutException
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/Inactivity.kt | within | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | made-flag | a tick seen as the timeout fires is read again from the tick count (ticks.value) before the timeout counts; the settled flag decides who ends the block
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/KeptWithin.kt | keptWithin | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | completedWithin | the helper itself: kept is set as the block returns, with no suspension point in between, so a result returned as the timeout fires is the result (completedWithin for a block that may give null)
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/KuicksilverEngine.kt | awaitResolutions | withTimeoutOrNull | 2 | made-flag | resolved is set inside the scope as the resolutions are read, so the connect timeout firing then (also as the scope completes) keeps them; the second wait only joins the record jobs, read after it
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/KuicksilverEngine.kt | checkNetwork | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | awaits the first network report, a Deferred that keeps it
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/KuicksilverEngine.kt | httpsUpgrade | withTimeoutOrNull | 2 | made-flag | decided is set inside the scope as the upgrade is decided, so the connect timeout firing then (also as the scope completes) keeps it; the second wait only joins the query, read after it
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/KuicksilverEngine.kt | lookupQuietly | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | side-effect-free | a lookup whose answer is kept in dns; the result is not used here
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ProtocolRace.kt | race | onTimeout | 1 | select-atomic | select of the HTTP/3 attempt's Deferred and the timeout: the Deferred keeps its outcome whichever clause wins
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ProxyResolverWindows.kt | run | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | made-flag | the call's Deferred is read after the wait: an answer that came as the bound fires is the answer, not Failed
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/RequestDns.kt | answered | onTimeout | 1 | select-atomic | the second family's answer is either taken by the select or left in its channel (CHANGELOG: "the other family's answer at the end of the Resolution Delay is used")
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/WebSocketLifetime.kt | boundByCloseWait | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | both branches end alike: a close job that completed as the close wait fires is cancelled, which does nothing to it
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/WebSocketLifetime.kt | runHandlers | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | made-flag | left tracks the handlers not run yet; the ones the bound cut off are started afterwards
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/dns/HttpsRecordCache.kt | start | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | made-flag | answer is set as the lookup returns: an answer that came as the query timeout fires is stored and given out
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/h1/H1Pool.kt | closeAll | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | joins the closers; nothing is taken
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/h1/H1Pool.kt | closeInOrder | withTimeoutOrNull | 4 | pure-wait | the steps after the server's close was read (completedWithin keeps that): close_notify, the pumps' stop, the drain, the FIN. A pumps' stop dropped as its bound fires only skips draining a socket whose server already ended its TLS stream (close_notify or its transport's end), so nothing but its FIN is left unread: the close is the same
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/h1/H1Pool.kt | closeOrderly | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | an orderly close bounded; the socket is closed in finally either way
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/h1/H1Pool.kt | exchangeOnce | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | an answer to Expect: 100-continue read as CONTINUE_TIMEOUT fires is taken for none and the body sent; RFC 9110 section 10.1.1 lets a client send the content without waiting for any answer, and readResponse still reads the final one
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/h1/H1Pool.kt | obtain | withTimeout | 1 | made-flag | conn and stream are set as the block returns: a connection or stream obtained as the connect timeout fires is handed out, not released
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/h1/H1Pool.kt | webSocketConnection | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | the wait only chooses between two working transports for a WebSocket: an HTTP/2 SETTINGS change seen as it fires picks HTTP/1.1, as one just after it would
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/h2/H2Pool.kt | closeAll | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | awaits the connections' close; they are closed hard after it either way
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/h2/H2WebSocket.kt | h2WebSocket | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | the close wait after this side's END_STREAM (the wait for the server's end uses completedWithin); its result is not used
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/h3/H3Pool.kt | connectWebTransport | withTimeout | 1 | made-flag | made is set inside the timeout; a handshake that completes as it fires is used (made != null), never orphaned
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/h3/H3Pool.kt | connectionEntryOnce | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | made-flag | made is set as the race returns: a connection made as the connect timeout fires is the connection (SetupTimedOut only when none was made)
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/h3/H3Pool.kt | goAwayAll | withTimeoutOrNull | 2 | pure-wait | a GOAWAY written within its bound; the result is not used
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/h3/H3Pool.kt | shareSameAddress | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | joins the other setups' Deferreds, which keep their outcome; match reads them after the wait
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/h3/H3Pool.kt | track | withTimeoutOrNull | 2 | pure-wait | waits for an exchange's end and writes a GOAWAY; the results are not used
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/h3/H3Pool.kt | webSocket | withTimeoutOrNull | 3 | pure-wait | the close steps after the server's end was read (completedWithin keeps that). The second close wait's drain, dropped as it fires, is followed by stopSending, which the QUIC core sends only for a receive half that still wants it (RecvStream.wantsStopSending): one read to its FIN sends nothing
kuicksilver-ktor-network/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/network/HappyEyeballs.kt | timer | timer | 1 | side-effect-free | the attempt-delay timer only sends a race event; cancelled with the race, it takes nothing
kuicksilver-ktor-network/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/network/SocketTls.kt | close | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | both branches end alike: a socket job that completed as the bound fires gets abortTls, which does nothing to a closed session
kuicksilver-ktor-network/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/network/SocketTls.kt | failTls | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | the steps after a fatal alert (flush, pumps, linger, close); null aborts what is ending anyway
kuicksilver-ktor-network/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/network/SocketTls.kt | lingerAfterAlert | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | discards the peer's bytes after an alert; they are not wanted
kuicksilver-ktor-network/src/jvmCommonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/network/KslNioSocket.kt | close | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | both branches end alike: a writer that drained as the bound fires is cancelled, which does nothing to a finished job
kuicksilver-ktor-network/src/jvmCommonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/network/KslNioSocket.kt | selectOnce | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | waits for the selector to release a key; nothing is consumed
kuicksilver-ktor-network/src/nativeMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/network/TcpSockets.native.kt | await | withTimeoutOrNull | 2 | pure-wait | awaits a readiness Deferred kept in select for the next turn; a readiness dropped at the deadline is found again
kuicksilver-ktor-network/src/nativeMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/network/TcpSockets.native.kt | awaitConnectedWith | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | awaits a readiness Deferred kept in pending; the socket's state is read after the wait either way
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/Http2Serving.kt | closeWhenIdle | withTimeoutOrNull | 2 | pure-wait | watches a StateFlow of requests taken and awaits the close; nothing is consumed
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/Http2Serving.kt | drainsWhileMoving | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | awaits the close, polled for progress; nothing is consumed
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/Http2Serving.kt | serveH2 | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | the wait for the close after a GOAWAY: a connection that closed as it fires is aborted, which does nothing to a closed one
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/KuicksilverApplicationEngine.kt | stopIdentityWatcher | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | joins a cancelled watcher
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/KuicksilverApplicationEngine.kt | stopSuspend | withTimeoutOrNull | 2 | pure-wait | both branches end alike: a server job that ended as the grace period fires is cancelled (a no-op) and stopWasForcedForTest is set; the second join's result is not used
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/TcpListener.kt | closeWithin | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | both branches end alike: a socket job that ended as the bound fires is cancelled, which does nothing to it
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/TcpListener.kt | drainedWhileMoving | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | joins the socket's job, polled for progress
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/TcpListener.kt | releaseFailedPair | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | pure-wait | awaits an endpoint's close; null only logs
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/TcpListener.kt | withTimeoutOrRelease | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | made-flag | made is set inside the block and released when the deadline fired: a TLS handshake that completes as the request-head deadline fires ends the connection either way, since that deadline counts from accept and leaves the first head or preface no time
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/h1/HeadLimitedInput.kt | awaitSource | select-cancel | 1 | pure-wait | awaitContent takes no bytes (the select's cancel stops a wait, never a read); the content stays in the channel
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/h1/HeadLimitedInput.kt | awaitSource | withTimeoutOrNull | 1 | made-flag | arrived is set as the wait returns: body bytes that arrived as the body deadline fires are read, not a RequestBodyTimeout
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonMain/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/h1/ServerPipeline.kt | awaitRequestStart | select-cancel | 1 | side-effect-free | cancels an awaitContent when the server drains; awaitContent takes no bytes
